# .spool/lsp/lsp.req

feature: LSP

requirements:
  - id: LSP-1
    title: Go to Definition from Test Annotation
    description: >
      The LSP server must support navigating from a Spool ID
      annotation in a test file to the acceptance criterion
      definition in the corresponding .req file.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-28
    rationale: >
      Bidirectional navigation between tests and requirements
      is the primary value proposition of the LSP layer. Jumping
      from a test annotation to the AC definition lets developers
      quickly understand what a test is verifying.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: LSP-1-1
        title: Annotation Resolves to AC Definition
        description: >
          Given a test file with a Spool ID annotation referencing
          a known AC,
          when go-to-definition is invoked on that annotation line,
          then the LSP returns a location pointing to the AC's
          line in the .req file.

      - id: LSP-1-2
        title: Unknown Annotation Returns Empty
        description: >
          Given a test file with a Spool ID annotation referencing
          an unknown AC,
          when go-to-definition is invoked on that annotation line,
          then the LSP returns an empty result.

      - id: LSP-1-3
        title: Non-Annotation Line Returns Empty
        description: >
          Given a cursor on a line that is not a Spool ID annotation,
          when go-to-definition is invoked,
          then the LSP returns an empty result.

  - id: LSP-2
    title: Go to Definition from AC to Tests
    description: >
      The LSP server must support navigating from an acceptance
      criterion ID in a .req file to the test function(s)
      that cover it.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-28
    rationale: >
      Navigating from an AC to its covering tests lets developers
      verify coverage and jump directly to the relevant test code
      from the requirements specification.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: LSP-2-1
        title: AC Resolves to Test Locations
        description: >
          Given a .req file with an AC that has linked tests,
          when go-to-definition is invoked on the AC's id line,
          then the LSP returns locations for all linked test
          functions.

      - id: LSP-2-2
        title: Untested AC Returns Empty
        description: >
          Given a .req file with an AC that has no linked tests,
          when go-to-definition is invoked on the AC's id line,
          then the LSP returns an empty result.

      - id: LSP-2-3
        title: Non-ID Line Returns Empty
        description: >
          Given a cursor on a line in a .req file that does not
          contain a Spool ID,
          when go-to-definition is invoked,
          then the LSP returns an empty result.

  - id: LSP-3
    title: Server Lifecycle
    description: >
      The LSP server must implement the standard LSP lifecycle
      protocol over stdio JSON-RPC.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-28
    rationale: >
      Standard LSP lifecycle compliance ensures compatibility
      with all major editors (VS Code, Neovim, etc.) without
      requiring editor-specific adapters.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: LSP-3-1
        title: Initialize Returns Capabilities
        description: >
          Given an initialize request with a rootUri,
          when the server processes it,
          then it returns capabilities including
          definitionProvider set to true.

      - id: LSP-3-2
        title: Reindex on Save
        description: >
          Given a textDocument/didSave notification,
          when the server processes it,
          then the traceability index is rebuilt from disk.

  - id: LSP-4
    title: Document Links
    description: >
      The LSP server must provide clickable document links for
      Spool IDs in both .req files and test files, enabling
      ctrl+click navigation.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-28
    rationale: >
      Document links make Spool IDs visually identifiable as
      navigable references, providing a more discoverable UX
      than go-to-definition alone.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: LSP-4-1
        title: Req File Links to Tests
        description: >
          Given a .req file with an AC that has linked tests,
          when the document is opened,
          then the AC's ID appears as a clickable link targeting
          the covering test.

      - id: LSP-4-2
        title: Untested AC Has No Link
        description: >
          Given a .req file with an AC that has no linked tests,
          when the document is opened,
          then the AC's ID does not appear as a clickable link.

      - id: LSP-4-3
        title: Test Annotation Links to AC
        description: >
          Given a test file with a Spool ID annotation referencing
          a known AC,
          when the document is opened,
          then the annotation appears as a clickable link targeting
          the AC definition in the .req file.

      - id: LSP-4-4
        title: Unknown Annotation Has No Link
        description: >
          Given a test file with a Spool ID annotation referencing
          an unknown AC,
          when the document is opened,
          then the annotation does not appear as a clickable link.

      - id: LSP-4-5
        title: Non-Annotation Lines Have No Links
        description: >
          Given a test file where a line is not a Spool ID annotation,
          when the document is opened,
          then that line does not produce a document link.

  - id: LSP-5
    title: Diagnostics
    description: >
      The LSP server must publish warning diagnostics for untested
      acceptance criteria and orphaned test annotations.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-28
    rationale: >
      Inline warnings surface coverage gaps directly in the editor
      without requiring the developer to run the CLI.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: LSP-5-1
        title: Untested AC Warning
        description: >
          Given a .req file with an active AC that has no covering tests,
          when the index is built,
          then a warning diagnostic is published on the AC's id line.

      - id: LSP-5-2
        title: Orphaned Annotation Warning
        description: >
          Given a test file with a Spool ID annotation that does not
          match any known AC,
          when the index is built,
          then a warning diagnostic is published on the annotation line.

      - id: LSP-5-3
        title: Tested AC Has No Warning
        description: >
          Given a .req file with an AC that has covering tests,
          when the index is built,
          then no diagnostic is published for that AC.

      - id: LSP-5-4
        title: Clean Index Has No Diagnostics
        description: >
          Given a project where all active ACs have tests and all
          annotations reference known ACs,
          when the index is built,
          then no diagnostics are published.

  - id: LSP-6
    title: Code Lenses
    description: >
      The LSP server must provide code lenses showing test coverage
      counts on ACs in .req files and AC references on test
      annotations.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-28
    rationale: >
      Code lenses make traceability visible at a glance without
      requiring hover or navigation, showing coverage status
      inline above each AC and test annotation.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: LSP-6-1
        title: Tested AC Shows Test Count
        description: >
          Given a .req file with an AC that has linked tests,
          when code lenses are requested,
          then a lens appears showing the test count with a
          command to navigate to the tests.

      - id: LSP-6-2
        title: Untested AC Shows Untested Lens
        description: >
          Given a .req file with an AC that has no linked tests,
          when code lenses are requested,
          then a lens appears showing "untested".

      - id: LSP-6-3
        title: Test Annotation Shows AC Reference
        description: >
          Given a test file with a Spool ID annotation referencing
          a known AC,
          when code lenses are requested,
          then a lens appears showing the AC title with a command
          to navigate to the AC definition.

      - id: LSP-6-4
        title: Unknown Annotation Has No Lens
        description: >
          Given a test file with a Spool ID annotation referencing
          an unknown AC,
          when code lenses are requested,
          then no lens is produced for that annotation.

  - id: LSP-7
    title: Hover Information
    description: >
      The LSP server must provide rich hover tooltips for Spool IDs
      showing AC details and test coverage information.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-28
    rationale: >
      Hover info gives developers context about an AC or test
      relationship without navigating away from the current file.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: LSP-7-1
        title: Test Annotation Hover Shows AC Details
        description: >
          Given a test file with a Spool ID annotation referencing
          a known AC,
          when hover is invoked on that annotation,
          then the tooltip shows the AC title, description, and
          parent requirement.

      - id: LSP-7-2
        title: Unknown Annotation Returns No Hover
        description: >
          Given a test file with a Spool ID annotation referencing
          an unknown AC,
          when hover is invoked on that annotation,
          then no tooltip is shown.

      - id: LSP-7-3
        title: Non-Annotation Returns No Hover
        description: >
          Given a cursor on a non-annotation line in a test file,
          when hover is invoked,
          then no tooltip is shown.

      - id: LSP-7-4
        title: Req File AC Hover Shows Test Coverage
        description: >
          Given a .req file with an AC that has linked tests,
          when hover is invoked on the AC's id line,
          then the tooltip shows the test function names and files.

      - id: LSP-7-5
        title: Req File Untested AC Hover
        description: >
          Given a .req file with an AC that has no linked tests,
          when hover is invoked on the AC's id line,
          then the tooltip shows "No covering tests".

      - id: LSP-7-6
        title: Req File Non-ID Line Returns No Hover
        description: >
          Given a cursor on a line in a .req file that does not
          contain a Spool ID,
          when hover is invoked,
          then no tooltip is shown.
